# From the tests of the first compiler: src/lexer.rs, `character_literals`.
==== 1
---- file a.azl (no newline at end)
'
---- run lex a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout (empty)
---- stderr
error[E0104]: a character literal holds one ASCII character, as in `'a'`
 --> a.azl:1:1
  |
1 | '
  | ^
---- asserted 1:1 a character literal holds one ASCII character, as in `'a'`
